stimuli.content:
In a certain code:
'P % Q' means 'P is the daughter of Q';
'P & Q' means 'P is the husband of Q';
'P ! Q' means 'P is the father of Q'.

questions.question_text:
In a certain code:
'P @ Q' means 'P is the brother of Q';
'P # Q' means 'P is the mother of Q';
'P $ Q' means 'P is the daughter of Q'.

If 'A @ B # C $ D', which of the following is NOT true?

In a certain code:
'A © B' means 'A is the mother of B';
'A ® B' means 'A is the brother of B';
'A ™ B' means 'A is the daughter of B'.

Which of the following expressions definitely means that P is the niece of S?

Refer to the Cheques table. Which cheques does this query return?

SELECT chq_no FROM Cheques
WHERE amount > ALL (SELECT amount FROM Cheques WHERE status = 'Returned');

Refer to the Cheques table. What value does this query show in the diff column for cheque C108?

SELECT chq_no, amount - LAG(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY acc_no ORDER BY presented_on, chq_no) AS diff
FROM Cheques;
